# CHAPTER III

## PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES

#### Article 3

Protection of women and children from acts of violence and discrimination shall be conducted based on the principles of:
a. respect for human rights;  
b. justice and gender equality;  
c. non-discrimination;  
d. protection of victims;  
e. empowerment; andf. integration.

#### Article 4

The objectives of protection of women and children from acts of violence and discrimination are:
a. to prevent acts of violence and discrimination against women and children including trafficking in persons;  
b. to eliminate all forms of violence, discrimination, and exploitation against women and children;  
c. to protect women and children from acts of violence and discrimination in obtaining their legitimate rights constitutionally;  
d. to protect and provide a sense of security for women and children;  
e. to provide services and protection to women and children who are victims of acts of violence and discrimination, reporters, and witnesses; andf. to facilitate and conduct mediation on domestic disputes to realize the integrity of a harmonious and prosperous household.

##### CHAPTER….  

D:\PERDA PDF\2-PERDA PERLINDUNGAN HAK PEREMPUAN DAN ANAK.doc 6

##### HEAD OF DPPAS BELITUNG REGENCY

# CHAPTER IV

## FORMS OF VIOLENCE

#### Article 5

Forms of violence against women and children include: a. physical violence;  
b. psychological violence;  
c. sexual violence;  
d. neglect;  
e. coercion/deprivation of liberty;  
f. exploitation;  
g. threat of certain actions; and/orh. other violence.

# CHAPTER V

## RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE

#### Article 6

Women and children victims of acts of violence shall receive the following rights:
a. the right to have their dignity respected as human beings; b. the right to recovery of health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by victims;  
c. the right to determine their own decisions;  
d. the right to obtain information;  
e. the right to confidentiality;  
f. the right to compensation;  
g. the right to social rehabilitation;  
h. the right to complaint handling;  
i. the right of victims and their families to obtain facilities in the judicial process; andj. the right to assistance.

#### Article 7

Child victims of acts of violence, in addition to receiving the rights as referred to in Article 6, shall also receive special rights as follows:
a. the right to respect and full use for survival, growth, and development;  
b. the right….  

D:\PERDA PDF\2-PERDA PERLINDUNGAN HAK PEREMPUAN DAN ANAK.doc 7
b. the right to basic services;  
c. the right to equal protection;  
d. the right to be free from various stigma; ande. the right to obtain freedom.

# CHAPTER VI

## OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES

#### Article 8

Obligations and responsibilities in providing protection to women and children from acts of violence are the shared responsibility of:
a. regional government;  
b. society;  
c. family; andd. parents.

#### Article 9

1. The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in Article 8 letter a, include: a. implementing policies for the protection of women and children from acts of violence established by the government;  
b. establishing policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women and children from acts of violence; c. conducting cooperation in the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence; d. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence; e. allocating budget for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence in accordance with regional financial capacity; andf. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence.  
2. In order to carry out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regent shall establish programs and action activities for the protection of women and children in one Regional Action Plan as a basis for OPD and

##### UKPD….  

D:\PERDA PDF\2-PERDA PERLINDUNGAN HAK PEREMPUAN DAN ANAK.doc 8 UKPD in implementing the protection of women and children from acts of violence.  

3. The Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2), shall be set forth in the strategic plan of the OPD.  
4. Further provisions regarding the Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2), shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

#### Article 10

1. The obligations and responsibilities of society as referred to in Article 8 letter b, shall be conducted in the form of community participation.  
2. Forms of community participation as referred to in paragraph (1), include:a. preventing the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children;  
b. providing information and/or reporting acts of violence against women and children to law enforcement or authorized parties; andc. participating in the handling of victims of acts of violence. (3) Forms of community participation as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be carried out responsibly in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

#### Article 11

The obligations of family and/or parents as referred to in Article 8 letters c and d, who legally have full responsibility to prevent all forms of violence and protect women and children as family members.

#### Article 12

Every person who hears, sees, or knows of the occurrence of violence against women and children is obliged to make efforts in accordance with their capacity to:  a. prevent and stop the continuation of acts of violence;  
b. provide protection to victims;  
d. provide….  

D:\PERDA PDF\2-PERDA PERLINDUNGAN HAK PEREMPUAN DAN ANAK.doc 9
d. provide emergency assistance; and/ore. assist in the process of filing an application for protection order.

# CHAPTER VII

## PREVENTION OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE

#### Article 13

1. To prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children, the Regional Government shall conduct empowerment and awareness-raising to families, parents and the community by providing information, guidance, and/or counseling.  
2. In addition to empowerment and awareness-raising as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government shall undertake efforts as follows:a. increasing the number and quality of educational units both formal and non-formal;  
b. opening accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement, and social services;  
c. opening employment opportunities for women;  
d. building community participation and concern for the prevention of protection of women and children from acts of violence;  
e. building and providing a complete and easily accessible information system;  
f. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities, and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care about women and children; andg. opening complaint posts for the protection of women and children from acts of violence.

#### Article 14

1. Prevention of the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 13, shall be carried out….  

D:\PERDA PDF\2-PERDA PERLINDUNGAN HAK PEREMPUAN DAN ANAK.doc 10 carried out by OPD and UKPD whose duties and functions are in the fields of:
a. social affairs;  
b. health;  
c. education;  
d. manpower;  
e. women's empowerment and child protection;  
f. youth and sports;  
g. population and civil registration;  
h. mental and spiritual; andi. peace and order.  
2. Prevention of acts of violence by OPD and UKPD as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be carried out in an integrated and continuous manner based on the Regional Action Plan.  
3. In addition to the Regional Government, prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) must be carried out by:a. family and/or closest relatives;  
b. society;  
c. educational institutions;  
d. health institutions;  
e. social community institutions; andf. business world and other institutions.

